-- Care Chart week-by-week rebuild — Your Rhythm, Year Three Part 1 content, 2026-07-29.
--
-- Eighth batch of the postpartum week-by-week build, first of two parts
-- closing the entire rebuild. Covers postpartum weeks 105-130 (roughly
-- 2 years to 2 years 6 months). No schema changes needed beyond
-- migration_43 (mental_health_note, already added for Sustainable Rhythms
-- Part 2). Week-number convention unchanged: postpartum week 105 =
-- week_number 145, week 130 = week_number 170.
--
-- Batching confirmed with Roop via AskUserQuestion: this 52-week phase
-- ("Your rhythm, year three," weeks 105-156) split into two 26-week
-- batches, same size as every batch since Settling into Strength and
-- matching how Sustainable Rhythms was split. This is Part 1; Part 2
-- (weeks 131-156, week_number 171-196) will carry through to the third
-- birthday, closing the entire postpartum rebuild.
--
-- Claude drafted the full 26-week base version (see "Care Chart — Your
-- Rhythm Year Three Part 1 — Base Draft (Weeks 105-130).md"), continuing
-- every decision established in Sustainable Rhythms Part 2: no "Choose
-- your recovery route" block (delivery-type differences are long resolved
-- by two years postpartum); real, named coping techniques woven into every
-- week's Reset section per Roop's standing instruction on including mental
-- health methods in every draft; one dedicated general-wellbeing check-in
-- week (120, "How are you, really," continuing the established ~12-15-week
-- cadence from weeks 88/100 in the prior batch); and condition_notes on the
-- closing week (130, all four flags), matching the pattern every prior
-- batch's closing week has followed even when it wasn't the true end of
-- the whole phase.
--
-- **Different process this batch, flagged transparently.** Roop uploaded a
-- file back for review ("preview.md") that turned out to be byte-for-byte
-- identical to Claude's own base draft (diffed directly — 2421 lines,
-- zero differences) — the external AI-app review pass evidently didn't
-- happen this time, rather than silently treating it as reviewed. Flagged
-- this to Roop via AskUserQuestion; she confirmed locking Claude's own
-- base draft as final for this batch rather than waiting for a re-upload.
-- Content therefore carries the same verification standard as every prior
-- batch's *drafting* stage (grounded in this project's established,
-- already-verified claims — GDM/high-BP/thyroid/PCOS long-term follow-up
-- reminders match what's already been independently verified in earlier
-- batches, no new numeric/clinical claims introduced this batch requiring
-- fresh verification) but has not been through the second-AI-app review
-- pass every other batch in this series has had.
--
-- Content parsed programmatically from Claude's own markdown draft (not
-- hand-transcribed, and not pandoc-converted since no docx existed this
-- time — a new parser, parse_yr3p1.py, was adapted from parse_sr1.py's
-- dash-underlined-header format, matching the draft's own authored
-- structure) and round-trip validated via the same state-machine
-- SQL-literal parser used for every prior migration: 53 jsonb blocks, zero
-- errors. All 26 week_numbers (145-170) present, no gaps or duplicates.
-- Zero stray backslashes (checked programmatically). Parens and quotes
-- balanced.
--
-- Next batch: Your rhythm, year three Part 2 (postpartum weeks 131-156,
-- week_number 171-196) — closes the entire postpartum week-by-week rebuild
-- at the third birthday.

