  146,
  'postpartum',
  'Bigger Words, Bigger Negotiations',
  'More words means more negotiating — that''s growth, not defiance.',
  'Notice your own patience with the new back-and-forth her growing vocabulary brings.',
  'By two, many toddlers have a real vocabulary and start using it to negotiate, argue, and assert opinions — about clothes, food, everything. It''s a genuine developmental leap, and it can also be exhausting in a very specific, new way.',
  ARRAY['More back-and-forth negotiation over small daily decisions','A shift from physical tantrums to more verbal pushback','Pride in her growing communication, mixed with fatigue from the negotiating','A need for new strategies as old ones stop working']::text[],
  '{"focus": "Something that helps you find patience through repetition.", "tiers": {"heavy": "Slow neck and shoulder rolls — tension from negotiating all day settles there.", "steady": "A walk with music or a podcast, a mental break from words.", "feeling_good": "Whatever cardio or strength session helps you feel steady."}, "mood_adjustment": "If patience is thin from a day of negotiating, movement that doesn''t require decisions helps most.", "safety": "No specific caution this week."}'::jsonb,
  'No specific note this week.',
  'No specific note this week.',
  'No specific note this week.',
  'No specific note this week.',
