(
  147,
  'postpartum',
  'Potty Training, At Your Own Pace',
  'There''s no single right way to do this, or right time to start.',
  'If potty training is on your mind, approach it at whatever pace fits your child and your household.',
  'Potty training timelines vary enormously between children, and pressure from comparison — other kids, other families'' timelines — rarely helps. Whether you''re deep into it, just starting, or not ready yet, this week is about tuning out the noise and following what actually works for your child.',
  ARRAY['Pressure (external or self-imposed) around potty training timing','Frustration with setbacks, which are a completely normal part of the process','Relief when it clicks, even partially','No interest in starting yet, which is also completely fine']::text[],
  '{"focus": "No specific movement theme this week.", "tiers": {"heavy": "A few calming breaths after a frustrating accident or setback.", "steady": "A walk to decompress from the day''s ups and downs.", "feeling_good": "Whatever movement you enjoy this week."}, "mood_adjustment": "No specific note this week.", "safety": "No specific caution this week."}'::jsonb,
  'No specific note this week.',
  'No specific note this week.',
  'No specific note this week.',
  'No specific note this week.',
  '{"heavy_day": "If a setback feels heavy, remind yourself accidents are a completely normal, expected part of learning — not a sign anything''s going wrong.", "a_little_low": "Comparing your child''s timeline to others'' rarely helps — every child gets there at their own pace.", "okay": "Notice today''s progress (or lack of it) without needing a verdict on the whole process.", "good": "A good day of progress is worth genuinely celebrating, however small.", "really_good": "Enjoy a real milestone moment fully."}'::jsonb,
  'Potty training can be relentless in the moment — a few minutes to yourself after a hard stretch is legitimate, not indulgent.',
  'No specific note this week.',
  'Ask another parent who''s been through it what actually helped them — real experience beats generic advice here.',
